<body>
<main>
<p class="kicker">Public claim registry · v0.3 · released 2026-11-11</p>
<h1>Audit Register</h1>
<p>Executable checks for the Coppalini Architecture corpus. Each record names a source, a verifier, a receipt and a declared native reference. You download the artifact, check its hash, run one command and read the result. The page describes the checks; the artifacts are the evidence.</p>

<div class="strip" role="list">
<div role="listitem"><b>12/12 PASS</b><span>hash-gated kit cards</span></div>
<div role="listitem"><b>9 exact · 3 float</b><span>float cards at declared 1e-12</span></div>
<div role="listitem"><b>48/48 exact checks</b><span>W-0 15 · W-1 15 · NDA-3 18</span></div>
<div role="listitem"><b>8/8 verifiers</b><span>Suture Audit v0.2, source-bound</span></div>
<div role="listitem"><b>1 command</b><span><code>python3 kit.py</code></span></div>
</div>

<nav aria-label="On this page"><ul>
<li><a href="#criterion">Acceptance criterion</a></li><li><a href="#rerun">Re-run it</a></li><li><a href="#records">Five records</a></li><li><a href="#cards">Twelve cards</a></li><li><a href="#float">Where exact arithmetic is not used</a></li><li><a href="#scope">Scope</a></li><li><a href="#lineage">Method lineage</a></li><li><a href="#machine">For automated readers</a></li>
</ul></nav>

<h2 id="criterion">Acceptance criterion</h2>
<p>A card counts as verified when all three conditions hold:</p>
<ol>
<li>Every file in the card's manifest hashes to its recorded SHA-256. A changed or missing file reports <code>HASH-FAIL</code> and the card does not execute.</li>
<li>The verifier exits with code 0.</li>
<li>The verifier prints its required marker line, for example <code>PASS: magnetic cap</code>.</li>
</ol>
<p>Each card also declares its arithmetic domain (exact, or float with a stated tolerance) and its boundary, meaning what it does not check. The kit prints the claim, domain, command, result, scope and SHA-256 for every card.</p>
<p>Exact cards use Python integers and <code>Fraction</code>, SymPy, and number fields Q(ζ₇), Q(ζ₇, i), Q(√5), Q(√2, √3), Q(√2, √5) and the Gaussian rationals. Cards with negative controls feed the verifier inputs that must be refused and fail if any is accepted: S-2 has five, L-1 three, W-0 four (N1–N4), W-1 six (N1–N6), and NDA-3 four (N1–N4).</p>

<h2 id="rerun">Re-run it</h2>
<pre>sha256sum Validator_Kit_B2_v0_2.zip
# expect c0bb1552bbc7d6522546d6f67fbb31d825c500f47d272812d35768a17b3fa2bc
unzip Validator_Kit_B2_v0_2.zip &amp;&amp; cd Validator_Kit_B2_v0_2
sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS        # 29 entries
python3 kit.py                 # expect 12/12 PASS</pre>
<p>Requirements: Python 3, and numpy for card C-1. sympy is optional for the symbolic minor in S-5 and is required by the W-0 packet. The shipped receipt (<code>KIT_RECEIPT.md</code>, <code>KIT_RECEIPT.json</code>) was produced on Python 3.13.18 under Linux with sympy installed. To confirm the gate, change one byte in any manifest file and run again: the affected card reports <code>HASH-FAIL</code>.</p>
<p><a href="downloads/Validator_Kit_B2_v0_2.zip">Download the validator kit</a> · <a href="public-claim-registry-v0.3.json">Read the machine registry</a></p>

<h2 id="records">Five released records</h2>
<p>Registry record <code>S-5/05a</code> is the Suture Audit bundle of eight verifiers. Card <code>S-5</code> in the kit table is one of the twelve cards.</p>
<article class="rec" id="rec-B-2" aria-labelledby="h-B-2">
<h3 id="h-B-2">B-2 · Validator Kit B2 v0.2</h3>
<dl>
<dt>Status</dt><dd>Released · hash-bound · PASS</dd>
<dt>Exact result</dt><dd>12 hash-gated cards, 12/12 PASS: 9 exact-arithmetic cards and 3 floating-point cards at a declared 1e-12 tolerance. Card-level claims, domains and boundaries are listed in the card table below.</dd>
<dt>Native result</dt><dd>Per card; see the card table.</dd>
<dt>Provenance equations</dt><dd>Per card; see the card table.</dd>
<dt>Root closure at the seam</dt><dd>Shared root (Root identities, above), checked in cards F-1 and E-1.</dd>
<dt>Source artifact</dt><dd><a href="downloads/Validator_Kit_B2_v0_2.zip">downloads/Validator_Kit_B2_v0_2.zip</a></dd>
<dt>Artifact SHA-256</dt><dd><code class="h">c0bb1552bbc7d6522546d6f67fbb31d825c500f47d272812d35768a17b3fa2bc</code></dd>
<dt>Run</dt><dd><code>python3 kit.py</code></dd>
<dt>Depends on</dt><dd>Python 3. numpy for card C-1. sympy optional for the symbolic minor in card S-5.</dd>
<dt>Boundary</dt><dd>Each card retains its own domain and stated scope. The kit certifies declared mathematical and native-domain relations; laboratory records, where relevant, remain retained in their own named receipts. v0.2 declares card C-1&#x27;s float tolerance (atol 1e-12, rtol 0); all other card hashes are unchanged from v0.1.</dd>
</dl>
</article>
<article class="rec" id="rec-S-5-05a" aria-labelledby="h-S-5-05a">
<h3 id="h-S-5-05a">S-5/05a · Suture Audit v0.2</h3>
<dl>
<dt>Status</dt><dd>Released · hash-bound · PASS</dd>
<dt>Exact result</dt><dd>Eight source-bound verifiers PASS for the paired finite-carrier and regular-branch cards: rank D𝒮Π = 16 and the cap b &lt; |χ| on the regular branch; exact Fractions and number fields.</dd>
<dt>Native result</dt><dd>Suture Einstein–Maxwell reduction: exact regular-branch map Π ↦ (g, F_sol) with nontrivial fibre. Register status: CLOSED as a model-local equation realization; the empirical novelty gate is OPEN (Native-Contact Closure Register v0.5).</dd>
<dt>Provenance equations</dt><dd>SF.7, SF.9–SF.13a, SF.17; SD.5, SD.9–SD.11e, SD.12–SD.14b, SD.17, SD.20e–f, SD.28–SD.30. Addresses are equation tags in 05_suture_field.tex and 05a_suture_field_dynamics.tex.</dd>
<dt>Root closure at the seam</dt><dd>η̂ = G ⊕ I₂ ⊕ I₂ ⊕ I₂ and Ĉ = C ⊕ C ⊕ C ⊕ C (SF.7); stabilizer 𝔨 = Stab(η̂, Ĉ) ≅ 𝔰𝔬(1,1) ⊕ 𝔲(3) (SD.9–SD.10).</dd>
<dt>Source artifact</dt><dd><a href="downloads/Suture_Audit_v0_2.zip">downloads/Suture_Audit_v0_2.zip</a></dd>
<dt>Artifact SHA-256</dt><dd><code class="h">b2df5089e3e7e6ce6f6a7f673d8381ca86accc05d1379fb3b75e22696b088448</code></dd>
<dt>Run</dt><dd><code>cd source &amp;&amp; python3 verify_all.py</code></dd>
<dt>Depends on</dt><dd>Cited Lorentzian 2-form normal forms (named source dependency). Residual ledger R-1 through R-12.</dd>
<dt>Boundary</dt><dd>The regular-domain conditions rank D𝒮Π = 16 and b &lt; |χ| belong to the stated reduction; cited Lorentzian 2-form normal forms remain a named source dependency. A future apparatus comparison would be a measurement record, not a condition on the released Einstein–Maxwell reduction.</dd>
</dl>
</article>
<article class="rec" id="rec-W-0" aria-labelledby="h-W-0">
<h3 id="h-W-0">W-0 · Weinberg seam v0.2</h3>
<dl>
<dt>Status</dt><dd>Released · hash-bound · PASS</dd>
<dt>Exact result</dt><dd>15/15 exact symbolic checks (SymPy; checks W0-1 to W0-11 and negative controls N1–N4) of the tree-level mass matrix, vacuum stabilizer and neutral diagonalization. Declared reference: Q = T3 + Y, Y_φ = 1/2, φ0 = (0, v/√2)ᵀ, g, g′, v &gt; 0. The mass operator is derived as the Hessian of the Higgs kinetic term. The bracket operator (rank 3, kernel 3) and the mass operator (rank 3, kernel 1) are kept distinct.</dd>
<dt>Native result</dt><dd>Tree-level electroweak mass relation inside the received Standard Model representation and vacuum: M²_EW has rank 3, a one-dimensional photon kernel and an exact (Z, A) diagonalization. No numerical mixing angle, mass ratio or comparison. Register status: CLOSED as source-reference contact at the received selection.</dd>
<dt>Provenance equations</dt><dd>Q_em = T₃ + Y, Y_φ = ½, φ₀ = (1/√2)(0, v)ᵀ, g, g′, v &gt; 0.  (D_μφ₀)†D^μφ₀ = (v²/8)[g²((W¹)² + (W²)²) + (gW³ − g′B)²]; M²_EW is its Hessian in (W¹, W², W³, B).  Q_em annihilates φ₀; the photon direction (W³, B) = (g′, g) acts by gg′Q_em.  β_EW has rank 3 and kernel dimension 3.  Provenance: The Electroweak Seam v0.1 §§1–6; Electroweak Two-Operator Certificate v0.1 §§1–4; Empirical Input Register v0.1 §§8.1–8.4, §14 (cited sources not bundled).</dd>
<dt>Root closure at the seam</dt><dd>None at this card. W-0 is the received model with supplied g, g′, v; the root-side interface is W-1.</dd>
<dt>Source artifact</dt><dd><a href="downloads/W0_v0_2_packet.zip">downloads/W0_v0_2_packet.zip</a></dd>
<dt>Artifact SHA-256</dt><dd><code class="h">9fe1b3c4d66ab42d59cfb8d16fd0c0ca1e4bb3b6c393ec191fa3c9516e7b0431</code></dd>
<dt>Run</dt><dd><code>python3 -I verify_w0_weinberg_seam_v0_2.py</code></dd>
<dt>Depends on</dt><dd>Standard electroweak representation, vacuum, g, g′ and v as the declared native reference.</dd>
<dt>Boundary</dt><dd>The standard electroweak representation, vacuum, g, g′, and v are the declared native reference. The card verifies their tree-level mass relation; a new numerical or running-parameter result would require its own record.</dd>
</dl>
</article>
<article class="rec" id="rec-W-1" aria-labelledby="h-W-1">
<h3 id="h-W-1">W-1 · Electroweak carrier adapter v0.2</h3>
<dl>
<dt>Status</dt><dd>Released · hash-bound · PASS</dd>
<dt>Exact result</dt><dd>15/15 exact symbolic checks of the declared 𝔲(2) carrier map and the W±, Z, A coordinate map, with negative controls N1–N6. The card introduces no new particle parameter.</dd>
