<article class="rec" id="rec-NDA-3" aria-labelledby="h-NDA-3">
<h3 id="h-NDA-3">NDA-3 · Native Domain Adapter Atlas v0.3</h3>
<dl>
<dt>Status</dt><dd>Released · hash-bound · PASS</dd>
<dt>Exact result</dt><dd>18/18 exact rational checks (Python Fraction only) of Body–SI–English length transport. The typed adapter admits a rational numeral with a typed unit and refuses a bare numeral, a time unit, a survey_foot tag and a foot_anatomical token (negative controls N1–N4). International foot = 381/1250 m as declared in the verifier. Row-specific institutional-contact labels are retained.</dd>
<dt>Native result</dt><dd>Exact SI–English length transport: 1 in = 127/5000 m, 1 ft_intl = 381/1250 m = 0.3048 m, 1 yd = 1143/1250 m, 1 fur = 25146/125 m, 1 mi = 201168/125 m. Authorities named in the register: BIPM metre definition; NIST HB 44 and NIST Guide conversion factors. Register status: CLOSED as exact conventional unit/language transport; a body reading keeps its own calibration and uncertainty record.</dd>
<dt>Provenance equations</dt><dd>B_ℓ —ρ_cal→ L_SI ⇄(T_exact) L_EN.  T_exact: 𝒬_ℓ^EN → ℚ·m, one-to-one and onto at the declared rational-record resolution; two typed expressions are equivalent exactly when their rational metre values agree.</dd>
<dt>Root closure at the seam</dt><dd>No root-algebra element enters at this seam. The closure is the typed 1:1 carrier 𝒬_ℓ^EN/∼ → ℚ·m.</dd>
<dt>Source artifact</dt><dd><a href="downloads/NATIVE_DOMAIN_ADAPTER_ATLAS_v0_3.zip">downloads/NATIVE_DOMAIN_ADAPTER_ATLAS_v0_3.zip</a></dd>
<dt>Artifact SHA-256</dt><dd><code class="h">4075a5c57fe36a2977311ea58dad5181ed5b971859df390e797ed23ee6f8d075</code></dd>
<dt>Run</dt><dd><code>python3 -I run_all.py</code></dd>
<dt>Depends on</dt><dd>Declared native units. A later metrology result is a separate reference receipt for a new statement.</dd>
<dt>Boundary</dt><dd>The stated Body–SI–English transport is closed by the 18 rational checks. A later metrology result is a separate reference receipt for a new statement, not a condition on the conversion itself.</dd>
</dl>
</article>

<h2 id="cards">The twelve kit cards: result, provenance and root seam</h2>
<p>Three columns orient a formal reader at each check. <b>Native result</b> is the result the card establishes inside its declared domain; it is a statement within that jurisdiction and not a new prediction. <b>Formal provenance equations</b> are the equation addresses the verifier checks or reads: SF.n in <code>05_suture_field.tex</code>, SD.n in <code>05a_suture_field_dynamics.tex</code>, GL.n in <code>01_gravity_light.tex</code>, plus the verifier's own displayed identities. <b>Root closure at the seam</b> names the root-algebra identity at which the check closes. Where a source makes no such statement, the cell says so.</p>

<h3 id="root">Root identities</h3>
<p>The shared root (<code>common.tex</code>, <code>\sharedroot</code>), checked exactly in cards F-1 and E-1:</p>
<pre>Q = [[1,1],[1,0]],  Ω = [[0,1],[−1,0]],  C = −Ω
G = [Q,Ω] = [[−2,1],[1,2]],  H = G/√5,  S = (2Q − I)/√5
Q² = Q + I,  C² = −I,  G² = 5I,  H² = S² = I
H = CS,  SG = √5 Ω = −GS,  HC = −CH,  HCH = −C
L_s = e^{sS},  L_sᵀ G L_s = G,  H L_s H = L_{−s}</pre>
<p>Suture carrier built on it (SF.7): <code>η̂ = G ⊕ I₂ ⊕ I₂ ⊕ I₂</code> (signature (7,1)), <code>Ĉ = C ⊕ C ⊕ C ⊕ C</code>, <code>Ĥ = H ⊕ D ⊕ D ⊕ D</code> with D = diag(1,−1) (SF.8).</p>

