<h2 id="float">Where exact arithmetic is not used</h2>
<p>Three cards use floating point: S-6, S-7 and C-1. Each declares its tolerance in the card and in the manifest: 1e-12. C-1 states it explicitly as <code>atol=1e-12, rtol=0</code>. All three are hash-gated and run under the same acceptance criterion as the exact cards.</p>
<ul>
<li>S-6 is a numerical cross-check; its exact counterpart is S-3.</li>
<li>S-7 checks the root-algebra CHSH identity (2√2 at 45-degree settings, local deterministic maximum 2 over 16 enumerated assignments). The step from violation to the impossibility of local hidden variables is Bell's theorem, and the card contains no laboratory data.</li>
<li>C-1 checks the standard Tsirelson spectrum {−2√2, 0, 0, 2√2} in a declared two-level model.</li>
</ul>
<p>Version note: kit v0.1 ran C-1 with numpy's default <code>allclose</code> tolerances. v0.2 declares them. The other eleven card hashes are unchanged.</p>

<h2 id="scope">Scope</h2>
<ul>
<li>The cards verify declared mathematical relations in declared native domains. No card contains laboratory data.</li>
<li>The Suture image result is proved relative to cited Lorentzian 2-form normal forms. The magnetic cap is an exact regular-branch result.</li>
<li>Residuals R-1 through R-12 are published with the paired cards. Card S-8 names R-1 (theorem proof), R-2 (π̃ₐ first class) and R-3 (free action of k off two points) as open.</li>
<li>Source guards in S-3 and F-1 are token checks on the TeX files. They confirm that named statements are present; they do not verify them.</li>
<li>Verification is self-administered. Hash-gating establishes artifact identity. It is not third-party certification, accreditation or an independent audit.</li>
<li>A later calibration, apparatus receipt or new-number comparison is a new record. It does not withdraw the physical office of a relation already stated and checked.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Next records</h3>
<ul>
<li>Suture residual ledger R-1 through R-12 retains derivation-level precision and remains published with the paired cards.</li>
<li>Electroweak provenance and any new-number comparison extend W-0 and W-1 without undoing their verified native-domain relation.</li>
<li>Atomic reference and apparatus records bind future readings to named editions and instruments while retaining their disclosed model realizations.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="lineage">Method lineage</h2>
<p>Published precedents for the design. This work is not certified, accredited or evaluated under any of them.</p>
<ul>
<li>Certifying algorithms: McConnell, Mehlhorn, Näher and Schweitzer, <cite>Computer Science Review</cite> 5(2), 2011, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cosrev.2010.09.009">doi:10.1016/j.cosrev.2010.09.009</a>. Output accompanied by a witness that a short checker can validate.</li>
<li>ASME VVUQ 1-2022, <a href="https://www.asme.org/about-asme/standards/verification-validation-uncertainty">terminology for verification, validation and uncertainty quantification</a>. The cards are verification, meaning mathematical correctness. They are not validation against observation.</li>
<li>NIST <a href="https://csrc.nist.gov/files/pubs/fips/180-4/final/docs/fips180-4.pdf">FIPS 180-4</a> (Secure Hash Standard, 2015 edition) defines the SHA-256 used for every manifest. NIST has announced a revision of that standard.</li>
<li>Nosek, Ebersole, DeHaven and Mellor, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1708274114">The preregistration revolution</a>, PNAS 115(11), 2018. The same freeze-before-read rule governs empirical inputs in the corpus: prediction and acceptance rule are fixed before the held-out datum is read.</li>
</ul>

